// Oscillating.
//
// A reader sees x go 1, 2, 1 while two writers each write once. Lahav & Boker,
//   TOPLAS 2022, Ex. 3.7, over relaxed accesses.
//
// Asserted below, by source:
//   herd7 on the zoo's cat models, run on this program: SC forbids, TSO
//     forbids, Coherence forbids, RC11 forbids, RC17 forbids, OD-LSO forbids.
//   the zoo's equivalence and ordering edges:
//     VbD forbids. Equivalent to SC (zoo edge).
//     x86-TSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     ClightTSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     RC11z forbids. Equivalent to RC11 (zoo edge).
//     PC forbids. Coherence forbids it, and PC is stronger.
//     PRAM forbids. MR forbids it, and PRAM is stronger.
//     Causal forbids. PRAM forbids it, and Causal is stronger.
//     Slow forbids. Local forbids it, and Slow is stronger.
//   the models' definitions:
//     CC allows. CC is WRA with every access synchronising; herd7's wra.cat
//       allows this shape over release and acquire accesses.
//     Local forbids. A view is one order: seeing 1, 2, 1 needs one of the
//       writes twice.
//     POCausal forbids. Whichever write is arbitrated first, a later load that
//       has seen both returns it.
//     RYW allows. The reader wrote nothing.
//     MR forbids. The second and third loads have seen both writes and return
//       different ones.
//     MW allows. MW alone rejects nothing: a read sees only the write it read.
//     WFR allows. The reader writes nothing, and the writers read nothing.
//   Not asserted, for want of a verdict to check against: MRD. RA, SRA and WRA
//     are defined on release stores and acquire loads, and this program has
//     other accesses.
x := 0;
{
  x := 1
} ||| {
  r0 := x;
  r1 := x;
  r2 := x
} ||| {
  x := 2
}
%%
allow (r0 = 1 && r1 = 2 && r2 = 1) [CC, RYW, MW, WFR]
forbid (r0 = 1 && r1 = 2 && r2 = 1) [SC, VbD, TSO, x86-TSO, ClightTSO,
                                     Coherence, RC11, RC11z, RC17, OD-LSO, PC,
                                     PRAM, Causal, Slow, Local, POCausal, MR]
